  "data_note": "Exact numerical artist inputs in plotted units; no values have been digitised from a PDF or recomputed from curves.",
  "caption_latex": "\\textbf{Correlations persist across a longer bath network.} {Endpoint $zz$ and $yy$ correlations for four (a,b) and five (c,d) spins}, retaining uniform/weak-end losses and feedback off/on. {(c)} uses a tighter vertical scale to resolve the smaller five-spin signal. Weak-end number losses are $(0.04,0.36,0.36,0.04)\\omega_c$ for four sites and $(0.04,0.92/3,0.92/3,0.92/3,0.04)\\omega_c$ for five; uniform losses are $0.2\\omega_c$ at each site. Site 2 is controlled for $N=4$, and site 3 for $N=5$, with the gain and phase of Fig.~\\ref{fig:feedback3}. Solid curves and pointwise 95\\% bands are HOPS. Dotted four-spin references are finite-cavity master equations. Neither spin endpoint is actuated."
